module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.Chow.ComponentBranchOrderTransport
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.Chow.ComponentMultiplicityBranchIndexing

/-!
# The incidence of a branch on a component, read in a flat algebra over the chart local ring

Let `X` be a decent algebraic space over `S`, let `W` be an étale chart of `X` and let `u` be a
point of it. The branches of `X` at the image of `u` in a flat `𝒪_{W, u}`-algebra `A` — the
minimal primes of `A` — each lie on one irreducible component of `|X|`, namely
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.componentOfFlatBranch`. A closed subspace `Y ⊆ X` whose point set is an
irreducible component of `|X|` cuts out, in `A`, the ideal generated by the kernel of the stalk
map of the chart projection `W ×_X Y → W`. This file proves that a branch of `A` contains that
ideal **if and only if** the component it lies on is `|Y|`.

That equivalence is the hypothesis `hinc` of
`AlgebraicGeometry.natCast_ord_sub_eq_finsum_components_mul_of_le_iff`, which is the additivity
of the order of vanishing over the irreducible components with the two hypotheses `hItop` and
`hc` of `AlgebraicGeometry.natCast_ord_sub_eq_finsum_components_mul` derived rather than
assumed. It is the only thing that formula asks about the branch-to-component map, and it has no
dimension theory and no length theory in it: both directions are the single statement that the
point of `W` cut out by a branch lies in the preimage of `|Y|`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.componentIdeal_le_iff_componentOfFlatBranch`: for one closed
  subspace, a branch of `A` contains the ideal generated by the kernel if and only if it lies on
  that component.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.componentIdeal_le_iff_componentOfFlatBranch_of_proj_eq`: the same
  with the stalk at the projection of the chart point transported to the stalk at a point of `W`
  named in advance, which keeps the ideal a formula rather than an existential witness.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_componentIdeal_le_iff_componentOfFlatBranch`: the same with
  the ideal produced for a chart point of `W ×_X Y` lying over a point `u` given in advance, so
  that the ideal is an ideal of a flat algebra over `𝒪_{W, u}` for the one fixed `u`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_componentIdealFamily_le_iff_componentOfFlatBranch`: a family
  of such ideals for a family of closed subspaces all of whose point sets contain the image of
  `u`, inside the one ring `A`. This is `hinc` for a family.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_componentIdealFamily_le_iff_eq`: the same stated against the
  type of irreducible components of `|X|` through the image of `u`, which is the indexing in
  which the additivity formula is read: `I i ≤ 𝔮 ↔ c 𝔮 = i`.

## Implementation notes

The ideal is `Ideal.map` of the kernel along `algebraMap`, so one half of the equivalence is
`Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap`: containing the generated ideal is containing the kernel after
contraction along `𝒪_{W, u} → A`, and the contraction of a branch of `A` is the branch of
`𝒪_{W, u}` under it, which is by definition the prime that
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.componentOfFlatBranch` reads the component off. The chart-level
equivalence that remains is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.ker_stalkMap_closedSubspaceBaseChangeChartProj_le_iff`.

The ideals of a family are produced existentially rather than as a formula. Each closed
subspace `Y i` supplies its own point `w' i` of `W ×_X Y i` over the fixed `u`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_closedSubspaceBaseChangeChartProj_eq`), and the kernel of the
stalk map at `w' i` is an ideal of `𝒪_{W, W ×_X Y i → W of w' i}`, a ring equal to `𝒪_{W, u}`
only propositionally. Rather than carry that equality through the statements as a `stalkCongr`
isomorphism, the point equality is substituted inside the proof, which is possible exactly
because the ideal is not named in the statement.

No tag is claimed. The source has no numbered result here: this is the incidence bookkeeping
internal to the proofs of Stacks 0EQ2, 0EQA and 0EQQ, which all regroup a sum over the branches
of `X` at a point into a sum over the irreducible components of `X` through it.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 02QG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02QG)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EE9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EE9)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EQ2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EQ2)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EQA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EQA)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EQQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EQQ)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace

universe v u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

attribute [local instance] pointTopology

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
    {X : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u} (hX : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS X)
    (hdec : IsDecentSpace B S hS X)

/-! ### One closed subspace, at a point of its chart -/

section One

variable (Y : Subfunctor X) (hY : IsClosedSubspace B S hS Y)
    (hYcomp : subspacePointSet B S hS X Y ∈ irreducibleComponents (points B S hS X))
    (W : SmallEtale B S hS X)
    (w' : chartScheme (closedSubspaceBaseChangeChart B S hS hX Y hY W))

include hX hdec hYcomp in
/-- **A branch of a flat algebra over the chart local ring contains the ideal of a component if
and only if it lies on that component.** Let `Y ⊆ X` be a closed subspace whose point set is an
irreducible component of `|X|`, let `W` be an étale chart of `X`, let `w'` be a point of
`W ×_X Y` and let `A` be a flat algebra over the local ring of `W` at the projection of `w'`.
Then a minimal prime `𝔮` of `A` contains the ideal generated by the kernel of
`𝒪_{W, w'} ← 𝒪_{W ×_X Y, w'}`'s source — that is, the image in `A` of
`ker (𝒪_{W, w'} → 𝒪_{W ×_X Y, w'})` — if and only if the irreducible component of `|X|` on
which the branch `𝔮` lies is `|Y|`.

Containing the generated ideal is containing the kernel after contraction along
`𝒪_{W, w'} → A` (`Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap`), and that contraction is the branch of
`𝒪_{W, w'}` under `𝔮`, which is the prime
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.componentOfFlatBranch` is defined at; so this is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.ker_stalkMap_closedSubspaceBaseChangeChartProj_le_iff`. -/
theorem componentIdeal_le_iff_componentOfFlatBranch
    (A : Type v) [CommRing A]
    [Algebra ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk
      (closedSubspaceBaseChangeChartProj B S hS hX Y hY W w')) A]
    [Module.Flat ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk
      (closedSubspaceBaseChangeChartProj B S hS hX Y hY W w')) A]
    (q : {q : PrimeSpectrum A // q.asIdeal ∈ minimalPrimes A}) :
    (RingHom.ker ((closedSubspaceBaseChangeChartProj B S hS hX Y hY W).stalkMap w').hom).map
        (algebraMap ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk
          (closedSubspaceBaseChangeChartProj B S hS hX Y hY W w')) A) ≤ q.1.asIdeal ↔
      ((componentOfFlatBranch B S hS hX hdec W
          (closedSubspaceBaseChangeChartProj B S hS hX Y hY W w') A q).1 :
        irreducibleComponents (points B S hS X)).1 = subspacePointSet B S hS X Y := by
  have hp : (PrimeSpectrum.comap (algebraMap ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk
      (closedSubspaceBaseChangeChartProj B S hS hX Y hY W w')) A) q.1).asIdeal ∈
      minimalPrimes ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk
        (closedSubspaceBaseChangeChartProj B S hS hX Y hY W w')) :=
    StacksDraft.comap_mem_minimalPrimes_of_ringHom_flat _
      (RingHom.flat_algebraMap_iff.2 inferInstance) q.2
  rw [Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap, componentOfFlatBranch]
  exact ker_stalkMap_closedSubspaceBaseChangeChartProj_le_iff B S hS hX hdec Y hY hYcomp W w'
    ⟨_, hp⟩

include hX hdec hYcomp in
/-- **The same incidence, read at a point of the chart given in advance.** This is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.componentIdeal_le_iff_componentOfFlatBranch` with the stalk at the
projection of `w'` transported, along the canonical identification of stalks at equal points,
to the stalk at a point `u` of `W` named beforehand — so that the ideal is an ideal of a flat
algebra over `𝒪_{W, u}` for the one fixed `u` and *is still a formula in `w'`*.

The transported form is the one in which the ideal can be matched with the ideal of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.ringEquiv_henselianLocalRing_quotient_ker_stalkMap_rep_snd`, whose
chart is the same base change `W ×_X Y` but whose point of it is only known to lie over the
distinguished point of `W` — hence the transport. The existential
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_componentIdeal_le_iff_componentOfFlatBranch` cannot be used for
that, because it discards the ideal. -/
theorem componentIdeal_le_iff_componentOfFlatBranch_of_proj_eq (u : chartScheme W)
    (hu : closedSubspaceBaseChangeChartProj B S hS hX Y hY W w' = u)
    (A : Type v) [CommRing A] [Algebra ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk u) A]
    [Module.Flat ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk u) A]
    (q : {q : PrimeSpectrum A // q.asIdeal ∈ minimalPrimes A}) :
    (RingHom.ker (((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalkCongr (.of_eq hu.symm)).hom ≫
        (closedSubspaceBaseChangeChartProj B S hS hX Y hY W).stalkMap w').hom).map
        (algebraMap ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk u) A) ≤ q.1.asIdeal ↔
      ((componentOfFlatBranch B S hS hX hdec W u A q).1 :
        irreducibleComponents (points B S hS X)).1 = subspacePointSet B S hS X Y := by
  cases hu
  rw [show (((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalkCongr
      (Inseparable.of_eq (Eq.symm (rfl :
        closedSubspaceBaseChangeChartProj B S hS hX Y hY W w' = _)))).hom) = 𝟙 _ from
    TopCat.Presheaf.stalkSpecializes_refl _ _, Category.id_comp]
  exact componentIdeal_le_iff_componentOfFlatBranch B S hS hX hdec Y hY hYcomp W w' A q

end One

/-! ### The ideal of a component inside a flat algebra over the local ring at a given point -/

section AtPoint

variable (W : SmallEtale B S hS X) (u : chartScheme W)
    (A : Type v) [CommRing A] [Algebra ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk u) A]
    [Module.Flat ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk u) A]

include hX hdec in
/-- **The ideal in `A` cut out by a component, at a point of the chart given in advance.** Let
`Y ⊆ X` be a closed subspace whose point set is an irreducible component of `|X|`, let `u` be a
point of an étale chart `W` of `X` lying in the preimage of `|Y|`, and let `A` be a flat
`𝒪_{W, u}`-algebra. Then there is an ideal `I` of `A` such that a branch `𝔮` of `A` contains `I`
if and only if the component on which `𝔮` lies is `|Y|`.

`I` is the ideal generated by the kernel of the stalk map of `W ×_X Y → W` at a point of
`W ×_X Y` over `u`, which exists by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_closedSubspaceBaseChangeChartProj_eq`; the equivalence is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.componentIdeal_le_iff_componentOfFlatBranch`. The ideal is produced
existentially so that the point equality can be substituted rather than carried as a
`stalkCongr` isomorphism; see the module docstring. -/
theorem exists_componentIdeal_le_iff_componentOfFlatBranch
    (Y : Subfunctor X) (hY : IsClosedSubspace B S hS Y)
    (hYcomp : subspacePointSet B S hS X Y ∈ irreducibleComponents (points B S hS X))
    (hu : chartSchemeToPoints B S hS X W u ∈ subspacePointSet B S hS X Y) :
    ∃ I : Ideal A, ∀ q : {q : PrimeSpectrum A // q.asIdeal ∈ minimalPrimes A},
      I ≤ q.1.asIdeal ↔
        ((componentOfFlatBranch B S hS hX hdec W u A q).1 :
          irreducibleComponents (points B S hS X)).1 = subspacePointSet B S hS X Y := by
  obtain ⟨w', hw'⟩ := exists_closedSubspaceBaseChangeChartProj_eq B S hS hX Y hY W u hu
  subst hw'
  exact ⟨_, componentIdeal_le_iff_componentOfFlatBranch B S hS hX hdec Y hY hYcomp W w' A⟩

include hX hdec in
/-- **A family of component ideals inside one flat algebra over the chart local ring, with the
incidence of the branches.** Let `u` be a point of an étale chart `W` of `X`, let `A` be a flat
`𝒪_{W, u}`-algebra, and let `Y i ⊆ X` be closed subspaces whose point sets are irreducible
components of `|X|` all containing the image of `u`. Then there is a family of ideals `I i` of
`A` such that for every `i` and every branch `𝔮` of `A`

  `I i ≤ 𝔮` if and only if the component on which `𝔮` lies is `|Y i|`.

This is the hypothesis `hinc` of
`AlgebraicGeometry.natCast_ord_sub_eq_finsum_components_mul_of_le_iff` for a family, read with
the components named by the closed subspaces cutting them out; see
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_componentIdealFamily_le_iff_eq` for the form indexed by the
components themselves. -/
theorem exists_componentIdealFamily_le_iff_componentOfFlatBranch {ι : Type*}
    (Y : ι → Subfunctor X) (hY : ∀ i, IsClosedSubspace B S hS (Y i))
    (hYcomp : ∀ i, subspacePointSet B S hS X (Y i) ∈
      irreducibleComponents (points B S hS X))
    (hu : ∀ i, chartSchemeToPoints B S hS X W u ∈ subspacePointSet B S hS X (Y i)) :
    ∃ I : ι → Ideal A, ∀ (i : ι) (q : {q : PrimeSpectrum A // q.asIdeal ∈ minimalPrimes A}),
      I i ≤ q.1.asIdeal ↔
        ((componentOfFlatBranch B S hS hX hdec W u A q).1 :
          irreducibleComponents (points B S hS X)).1 = subspacePointSet B S hS X (Y i) :=
  by
  choose I hI using fun i => exists_componentIdeal_le_iff_componentOfFlatBranch B S hS hX hdec W u
    A (Y i) (hY i) (hYcomp i) (hu i)
  exact ⟨I, hI⟩

include hX hdec in
/-- **The family of component ideals indexed by the components themselves, with the incidence
hypothesis in the shape the additivity formula asks for.** Let `u` be a point of an étale chart
`W` of `X` and let `A` be a flat `𝒪_{W, u}`-algebra. Then there is a family of ideals `I i` of
`A`, indexed by the irreducible components `i` of `|X|` through the image of `u`, with

  `I i ≤ 𝔮` if and only if `componentOfFlatBranch 𝔮 = i`

for every branch `𝔮` of `A`. This is exactly the hypothesis `hinc` of
`AlgebraicGeometry.natCast_ord_sub_eq_finsum_components_mul_of_le_iff`, with the
branch-to-component map `c` of that formula taken to be
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.componentOfFlatBranch`.

Each component is cut out by the reduced induced closed subspace
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.integralClosedSubspaceOfComponent` on it, whose point set is the
component (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.subspacePointSet_integralClosedSubspaceOfComponent`); the
previous statement then gives the ideals, and the equality of components is the equality of
their point sets because an irreducible component of `|X|` through a point is determined by its
point set. -/
theorem exists_componentIdealFamily_le_iff_eq :
    ∃ I : {V : irreducibleComponents (points B S hS X) //
        chartSchemeToPoints B S hS X W u ∈ (V : Set (points B S hS X))} → Ideal A,
      ∀ (i : {V : irreducibleComponents (points B S hS X) //
          chartSchemeToPoints B S hS X W u ∈ (V : Set (points B S hS X))})
        (q : {q : PrimeSpectrum A // q.asIdeal ∈ minimalPrimes A}),
        I i ≤ q.1.asIdeal ↔ componentOfFlatBranch B S hS hX hdec W u A q = i := by
  obtain ⟨I, hI⟩ := exists_componentIdealFamily_le_iff_componentOfFlatBranch B S hS hX hdec W u A
    (fun i : {V : irreducibleComponents (points B S hS X) //
        chartSchemeToPoints B S hS X W u ∈ (V : Set (points B S hS X))} =>
      (integralClosedSubspaceOfComponent B S hS hX hdec i.1).subspace)
    (fun i => (integralClosedSubspaceOfComponent B S hS hX hdec i.1).isClosedSubspace)
    (fun i => by
      rw [subspacePointSet_integralClosedSubspaceOfComponent]
      exact i.1.2)
    (fun i => by
      rw [subspacePointSet_integralClosedSubspaceOfComponent]
      exact i.2)
  refine ⟨I, fun i q => (hI i q).trans ?_⟩
  rw [subspacePointSet_integralClosedSubspaceOfComponent]
  exact ⟨fun h => Subtype.ext (Subtype.ext h), fun h => congrArg (fun V => (V.1 :
    irreducibleComponents (points B S hS X)).1) h⟩

end AtPoint

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

end
